==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|proboscis}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} [[προβοσκίς]] "elephant's trunk," literally "means for taking food," from [[προ]] "forward" + [[βόσκειν]] "to nourish, feed," from [[βόσκεσθαι]] "graze, be fed," from the root *bot (compare [[βοτάνη]] "grass, fodder); more at [[botany]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/proʊˈbɒsɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es|proboscides}}

# {{label|en|anatomy}} An elongated tube from the head or connected to the mouth, of an animal.
## The tubular feeding and sucking organ of certain [[invertebrate]]s like [[insect]]s, [[worm]]s and [[mollusc]]s.
## The trunk of an [[elephant]].
# {{label|en|informal|mildly|jocular}} A large or lengthy human [[nose]].

====Derived terms====
* [[proboscis monkey]]

